3.Impact
After 44 hours Akira deployment began starting with encrypting the backup server. Remote execution was done from main
domain controller to encrypt network shares after that threat actor pivoted to the child domain and executed akira's binary 39 times
on the domain controller upon execution Akira deleted Volume Shadow Copies and leveraged WMI to trigger a PowerShell
command on every infected host.

4.Response and recovery
Used a backup from before the installation of BumbleBee loader, changed all administrative passwords, changed credentials in veeam PostgreSQL,
Invalidated sessions, invalidated tokens and API keys, reset krbtgt multiple times, every ioc was added to a firewall blocklist,
Restricted modifications and creation rights on program folders, configured gpo to monitor unexpected file modifications.

5.Post-incident actions
Perform an audit of AD configuration, Implement: Tiered Administration, WDAC policies, Microsoft Vulnerable Driver Blocklist for BYOVD,
Secure Web Gateway. Perform Security Awareness trainings focusing on SEO poisoning. Update Playbooks.
